# The old Eleventy site, which this one replaced in cbd2582. Every source below
# is a URL that site published, read off its permalinks in `git show cbd2582^1`,
# and every target is what took its place here. Permanent, and meant to stay:
# Google asks for a site move's redirects to be kept for at least a year, and a
# permanent redirect is the one that hands a page's standing to its successor.
# `scripts/check-dist.mjs` fails the build if a target stops resolving.
#
# A URL with nothing to succeed it is left out on purpose and answers 404.
# Sending it to the homepage would be a soft 404 by another name, so each gets a
# rule the day the client names a successor. The pages: the old five-step build
# method at `/aanpak/`, its four step pages under `/services/`, and
# `/customerzone/`. The files under /assets/: the demo videos `smartagents.mp4`
# and `smartspace-demo.mp4`; `handshake.webp`, a stock photo nothing here shows;
# `agent-network.svg`, a decoration on the old team page; `smartspace-ui.png`, a
# SmartSpace screen no current page shows; the SVG banners of the four posts
# deleted before the redesign (`wat-is-een-agent`, `rpa-vs-agents`,
# `case-claes-logistics`, `copilot-tips`); and the old decks' `deck/deck-stage.js`
# and `deck/tokens.css`. The old site's stylesheets and scripts under /shared/
# have nothing to succeed them either.
#
# Every page is here twice, with and without its trailing slash. Cloudflare's
# redirects doc writes `/trailing /trailing/ 301` as a rule of its own and never
# says one form matches the other, so the slashless URL a person types would
# otherwise reach the catch-all, which puts /nl/ in front of it and finds nothing.

